New opt-in option `--inherited-trait-axioms` (default off; `inherited-trait-axioms = true` in a project file): a bodiless ghost member of a trait that is marked `{:axiom}` (a lemma, a ghost method, a ghost function or predicate, or a two-state lemma, function or predicate, none of them extreme or static) is a trait axiom, and a class, datatype or newtype that extends the trait inherits it without implementing it (https://github.com/erniecohen/dafny/issues/89). An override is still checked. `dafny audit` lists each trait axiom and each type that inherits one without overriding it. Under the option, `{:axiom}` on a bodiless compiled or extreme trait member is an error unless the member is `{:extern}`, and a refinement may not add `{:axiom}` to a bodiless trait member of the module it refines. Whether a member is a trait axiom is fixed by the option in effect where it is declared, and a library and its client must agree on the option. With the option off nothing changes: such a type is rejected with "does not implement trait lemma", as before.
